<title>CANADA: CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - March 18.</title>
<headline>CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - March 18.</headline>
<text>
<p>WEEK OF MARCH 18 VERSUS MARCH 11, 1997		   DRILLING</p>
<p>	     MOVING  RIGGING  DRILLING   DOWN    TOTAL   YR AGO</p>
<p> ALBERTA    9/7     2/2     332/325    8/12   351/346    281</p>
<p> SASK.	1/0     0/0	68/66     0/0     69/66	30</p>
<p> B.C.	 0/0     1/1	57/62     0/1     58/64	40</p>
<p> N.W.T.     0/0     0/0	 2/3	4/3	6/6	  2</p>
<p> MAN.	 0/0     0/0	 1/2	0/0	1/2	  1</p>
<p> TOTAL     10/7     3/3     460/458   12/16   485/484    354</p>
<p>MOVING, RIGGING = CURRENTLY UNDER CONTRACT, BUT NOT AT FULL RATE. TOTAL LINE IS TOTAL WESTERN CANADA. FIGURES SUPPLIED BY CANADIAN ASSOCIATION OF OILWELL DRILLING CONTRACTORS.</p>
<p>((Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
